From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sat, 11 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: in Tag a monster of the partner is a Synchro material
 of the team, at n > 2

Owner rule [R-TAG-PARTNER-COST] (ADR-0002): "You may use your partner's cards for costs, Tributes, materials and summon conditions."
card::is_can_be_synchro_material refused a monster on the field when its controller was not the controller of the Synchro Monster
(raw compare, the stock rule that only the own monsters are material, unless EFFECT_SYNCHRO_MATERIAL). The Lua filter of the stock
procedure (proc_synchro.lua synchmatfilter) accepts `mc:IsControler(tp) or mc:IsCanBeSynchroMaterial(c)`, so a Tuner or a
non-Tuner of the partner was never a material. With more than two duelists the test is now "same team" (both are duelists and
share a team). Free for all has no partner: same_team is false for two different duelists, so nothing changes there. With two
duelists the stock compare is kept. EFFECT_SYNCHRO_MATERIAL (any field) is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
---
 card.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/card.cpp b/card.cpp
index 0ae15a8..7d43f4e 100644
--- a/card.cpp
+++ b/card.cpp
@@ -4010,8 +4010,14 @@ int32_t card::is_can_be_synchro_material(card* scard, uint8_t playerid, card* /*
 		return FALSE;
 	if(!(get_type(scard, SUMMON_TYPE_SYNCHRO, playerid) & TYPE_MONSTER))
 		return FALSE;
-	if(scard && current.location == LOCATION_MZONE && current.controler != scard->current.controler && !is_affected_by_effect(EFFECT_SYNCHRO_MATERIAL))
-		return FALSE;
+	if(scard && current.location == LOCATION_MZONE && !is_affected_by_effect(EFFECT_SYNCHRO_MATERIAL)) {
+		// More than two duelists (Tag): a monster of the partner is a Synchro material of the team ([R-TAG-PARTNER-COST]), like a
+		// monster of the own field. Free for all has no partner (same_team is false for two different duelists). Two duelists: stock test.
+		const auto& gf = *pduel->game_field;
+		if(gf.n_duelists == 2 ? current.controler != scard->current.controler
+		                      : !(gf.is_duelist(current.controler) && gf.is_duelist(scard->current.controler) && gf.same_team(current.controler, scard->current.controler)))
+			return FALSE;
+	}
 	if(is_status(STATUS_FORBIDDEN))
 		return FALSE;
 	effect_set eset;
